uClibc-ng 1.0.59, libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c: include
<unistd.h> so syscall() is declared when building against the hub's
2.6.30 kernel headers.

With the 2.6.30 headers __NR_clock_adjtime does not exist, so the
syscall(__NR_adjtimex, ...) branch is taken - and nothing in that
header set declares syscall() any more (modern headers pulled
<unistd.h> in transitively). Forced by the v29 shipped build's
KERNEL_HEADERS switch to the SDK's sanitized 2.6.30 tree; proven
necessary by the Phase 2 build (the only socket/time-family
compile failure of its class left after the kernel-headers
linux/socket.h guard patch).

Provenance: commit 1894925 (v29 shipped runtime).

--- a/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c
@@ -9,6 +9,11 @@
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <sys/timex.h>
 #include <time.h>
+/* Sengled edit (v29 shipped build): with the hub's 2.6.30 kernel
+ * headers __NR_clock_adjtime does not exist, so the syscall() branch
+ * below is taken - and nothing in that header set declares syscall()
+ * any more (modern headers pulled <unistd.h> in transitively). */
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 int adjtimex(struct timex *buf)
 {
